  "notes_context": "These notes were distilled from earlier work in this repository that passed verification. Follow them unless the code or CHANGELOG.md shows they no longer hold.\n- [at-0004] Money operations accept idempotency_key first: Every function that moves money or changes a payment, credit or invoice balance must accept keyword-only `idempotency_key=None` and check it first, before any state validation: scan `ledgerly.audit.events()` for an entry with the same key and return the original record without reapplying. Pass `idempotency_key` into the `audit.record(...)` call.\n  (learned from task E04 on ledgerly 1.0.0; source INC-204; relied on 0x, 0 passed, 0 failed)\n- [at-0001] Use BillingError with snake_case codes: Raise ledgerly.errors.BillingError with a snake_case code string for domain validation failures, e.g. \"invalid_state\", \"invalid_quantity\", \"negative_amount\"; include a short detail string as the second argument.\n  (learned from task E02 on ledgerly 1.0.0; relied on 2x, 1 passed, 1 failed)\n- [at-0002] Reject bool where int is required: When validating integer inputs, explicitly reject bool via isinstance(x, bool) before the int check, since True/False pass isinstance(x, int).\n  (learned from task E02 on ledgerly 1.0.0; relied on 2x, 1 passed, 1 failed)\n- [at-0003] Normalize datetimes with ensure_utc: In ledgerly, normalize any incoming datetime with `ensure_utc` from `ledgerly.clock` before comparing or doing arithmetic (see `current_period` in `ledgerly/subscriptions.py`).\n  (learned from task E03 on ledgerly 1.0.0; relied on 1x, 0 passed, 0 failed)\n- [at-0005] Refunds above 500.00 need second approver: Support-initiated refunds and credits above 500.00 require a second approver per finance policy FIN-2026-03: accept keyword-only `approved_by=None` and raise `BillingError(\"approval_required\")` when the amount exceeds the threshold and no approver is given. Amounts at or below 500.00 need no approval.\n  (learned from task E04 on ledgerly 1.0.0; source FIN-2026-03; relied on 0x, 0 passed, 0 failed)\n- [at-0006] Use Decimal with ROUND_HALF_UP for money: Compute money in ledgerly with `Decimal(str(x))` and quantize to `Decimal(\"0.01\")` using `ROUND_HALF_UP`; avoid float arithmetic and built-in `round` for cent rounding.\n  (learned from task E05 on ledgerly 1.0.0; relied on 0x, 0 passed, 0 failed)",
